### Page content (aligned with check + KS)
Grounded in `det-landmarks-required.check.js` and `components/layouts.py`:

- **Purpose:** One document-level `main`; `nav` when ≥2 outside-main wayfinding links; semantic `header`/`footer` when `.site-header`, `.landing-header`, `.ks-site-footer-region`, etc. are present; no duplicate banner/contentinfo.
- **Pass/fail signals:** All seven violation kinds from the check (`missing-main`, `duplicate-main`, `missing-nav`, `missing-banner`, `duplicate-banner`, `missing-contentinfo`, `duplicate-contentinfo`).
- **Before:** `div.site-header`, sidebar links without `nav`, `div.doc-main`, `div.ks-site-footer-region`.
- **After:** `a.skip-link`, `header.site-header`, `aside.forge-sidebar` + `nav.nav-scroll`, `main#main.doc-main`, `footer.ks-site-footer-region` with **Ksr**/**Ksf** hash attrs.
- **Evidence:** `landmarksReport` metrics and remediation steps tied to `analyze-website-ux.mjs`.

### Real KS classes used
`site-header`, `site-header-brand`, `site-header-content`, `forge-brand`, `forge-sidebar`, `nav-scroll`, `nav-section-label`, `nav-link`, `doc-main`, `forge-card`, `card-label`, `forge-support`, `ks-doc-breadcrumb`, `ks-site-footer-region`, `skip-link`, `landing-header`, `landing-header-navbar`, `fs-landing-main` (referenced in passing signals).

